<!--
     Merchandising pipeline (garment_merchandising): Inquiry -> Quotation ->
     Order Confirmation, one per style, plus a merchandiser workload task
     list. 2026 timeline: inquiries Jan 2026, quotations Feb 2026, order
     confirmations Mar 2026 (matching costing_tee/polo/hoodie's costing_date
     / negotiation dates in 02_costing_demo.xml).

     Note on person references: garment.merch.inquiry.assigned_merchandiser_id,
     garment.merch.quotation (no direct merchandiser field), garment.merch.
     order.confirmation.merchandiser_id/*_approver_id and garment.merch.task.
     assigned_to_id are all Many2one('res.users') — not garment.hr.employee —
     so, per the convention already established in 02_techpack_demo.xml /
     02_bom_demo.xml / 02_costing_demo.xml (no res.users demo records exist
     for the HR employees), they point at base.user_admin. The actual human
     merchandiser of record throughout this pipeline is Farhana Akter
     (emp_merchandiser, Senior Merchandiser / Merchandising dept. manager per
     01_hr_demo.xml) — named explicitly in each record's description/remarks
     text so the story stays attributed to her even though the technical
     "owner" field is the seed Administrator user.

     FOB prices quoted below are taken from the computed garment.costing
     fob_price on costing_tee/costing_polo/costing_hoodie (material_cost 0 +
     cm_cost + overhead_cost + additional_cost_total, +10%/+10%/+12% margin
     per 02_costing_demo.xml): tee $3.20, polo $4.32, hoodie $8.50.
-->
